# A scripted panel walk, for developing the UI away from the cabinet.
#   ipacconf.py serve --fake-device fixtures/ipac2-1.55-keyboard.json \
#                     --fake-input fixtures/input-keyboard-mode.jsonl
# "after" is seconds to wait before the event. Name a board action and it is
# turned back into the keycode the kernel would have reported, so the whole
# translation path runs; or give raw evdev "type"/"code" numbers instead.
# The actions here are the factory MAME layout, so each one should light up
# the pin named beside it.
# The type 4 lines are EV_MSC scan codes: on a real keyboard node one shadows
# every press. They are here so the "say it once, then hide them" path runs -
# the script loops, so a single line across several passes is the proof.
{"after": 1.0, "type": 4, "code": 4, "value": 458756}
{"after": 0.0, "action": "UP", "value": 1}
{"after": 0.25, "action": "UP", "value": 0}
{"after": 0.6, "action": "LEFT", "value": 1}
{"after": 0.25, "action": "LEFT", "value": 0}
{"after": 0.6, "action": "CTRL L", "value": 1}
{"after": 0.3, "action": "CTRL L", "value": 0}
{"after": 0.6, "action": "ALT L", "value": 1}
{"after": 0.3, "action": "ALT L", "value": 0}
